---
title: One Pot Vegetable Tortellini Soup
servings: 4
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
author: Stella Drivas
source: https://hungryhappens.net/one-pot-vegetable-tortellini-soup/
source.name: Hungry Happens
tags: [soup, vegetarian, pasta, one-pot]
---

== Prep Ahead: For the Base ==

Dice @carrots{4}, @sweet onion{1}, @celery{4%ribs}, and @mushrooms{12%oz}.

Mince @garlic{4%cloves}.

== Prep Ahead: For the Seasoning ==

Measure @paprika{1%tsp} and @Italian herb seasoning{1%tbsp} into one bowl.

Measure @tomato paste{2%tbsp}.

== Prep Ahead: For the Finish ==

Grate @parmesan cheese{1/2%cup}, plus a little extra for topping if you like.

Measure @heavy cream{1/2%cup}.

Roughly chop @kale{3%handfuls}.

== Cooking Day ==

Heat @olive oil{1/4%cup} in a #large pot{} over high heat. Add the @carrots{} and @sweet onion{} and sauté for ~{3%minutes}.

Add the @mushrooms{} and @celery{} and sauté for several minutes. Stir in the @garlic{} for ~{30%seconds}.

Add the spice blend, @salt{}, @black pepper{}, and the @tomato paste{}; stir to coat.

Pour in @dry white wine{1/2%cup} and @vegetable broth{7%cups} and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer, cover, and cook for ~{20%minutes} until the carrots are tender.

Add @cheese tortellini{1.5%lb} and the grated @parmesan cheese{}; boil for ~{5%minutes}.

Gently stir in the @heavy cream{} and @kale{}.

Serve topped with a little freshly grated @parmesan cheese{} and a drizzle of @olive oil{}, if you like.

> Baby spinach or roughly chopped Swiss chard can stand in for the kale. Milk can replace the heavy cream, or leave it out. Gnocchi or a small pasta works in place of the tortellini, and extra broth can replace the wine.
